WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.763
The reader collects the
root key's start time,

2
00:00:02.763 --> 00:00:07.455
every managed account with its password
retrievers and migration state, and,

3
00:00:07.455 --> 00:00:12.587
for a delegated conversion, the domain
controllers and each host's operating system.

4
00:00:12.587 --> 00:00:14.013
Then ten rules run.

5
00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:18.877
Some come from Learn: the root key must
exist and be old enough, the migration's

6
00:00:18.877 --> 00:00:23.587
limits must hold, and managed accounts
shouldn't sit in privileged groups.

7
00:00:23.587 --> 00:00:27.641
Others come from the project plan:
every account needs a decision,

8
00:00:27.641 --> 00:00:30.194
an owner for its service principal names,

9
00:00:30.194 --> 00:00:34.624
an end date inside the program's
deadline, and a reconciled destination.

10
00:00:34.624 --> 00:00:39.789
The account standard adds three checks: a
new name must follow the naming standard,

11
00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:43.965
a group account's retrievers must
be exactly one group of its hosts,

12
00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:47.687
and a write with no SailPoint
request or ServiceNow change

13
00:00:47.687 --> 00:00:50.800
isn't planned at all; the
plan records it as blocked.

14
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.970
Every finding gets a stable ID.
